n    - VER-APPLY-01 to APPLY-07 and APPLY-09 to APPLY-18 match.\n    - `version` creates and stages `Cargo.lock` when none is tracked (run: `A  Cargo.lock`).\n    - `--emit-decision` with `--dry-run` is rejected with E276.\n    - `--emit-decision` with no bumps fails with E160 and writes nothing.\n  - **Reads:** VER-READ-04 (E315) matches (`callisto-model/src/vcs/mod.rs:37`).\n  \n  ## Unverified (read, not exercised)\n  - **VER-READ-01 to READ-03:** strict-fs and git \"not found\" handling was not exercised. READ-03's once-per-tag dedupe is only implied by `tags.rs:126`.\n  - **VER-GRP-05:** platform manifests and `optionalDependencies` pins were read in `commands/version.rs:713-785`, not run.\n  - **VER-CAS-05:**\n    - The pnpm `workspace:` explicit-range, alias and relative-path coverage matches `callisto-model/src/dependency.rs:60-125`, but npm and Python-lockfile fixtures were not run.\n    - The code applies that logic to every `WorkspaceKind` (pnpm, yarn, npm), not only pnpm.\n  - **VER-APPLY-13 and APPLY-16:** the E121 logic was read, not run.\n  - **VER-APPLY-14:** the npm, pnpm, yarn, bun and Python refresh commands match the code but were not run.\n  - **VER-AGG-06 in `mode: exit`:** `agg.consumed` is empty when no changesets exist, so the empty-changeset warning may fire even though stable finalization still bumps. I did not test it.\n  \n  ## Incident\n  One scratch script ran its `callisto` and git commands inside the worktree because another agent had deleted my scratch directory. Nothing was written. The plan was empty, `git commit` reported \"nothing to commit\", and `commands/version.rs` bailed with E160. The worktree now shows ` M docs/specs/cli.json` and ` M docs/specs/matrix.json`. Those were not made by me.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"I checked all 62 criteria in docs/specs/versioning.json against code, docs/errors.md and the v0.14.0 binary. Eight have drift. None is a wrong error code, a nonexistent code, a wrong flag or key name, 