{"parentUuid":"46961119-bdaf-407f-b383-5f9c4bfbd35f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fdaba07c-479e-42b3-b532-6f24a7e8d57d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01USzwRw9odMSMjD6cRLiRKd","type":"tool_result","content":"## VER-CS-07\n57-      \"criterion\": \"Writing fails for an empty summary with entries (E056), an empty package name (E057), or a name containing `\\\"`. A changeset with no entries and no summary writes as an empty file.\",\n## VER-APPLY-08\n258-      \"criterion\": \"Outside pre mode, `version` refreshes affected lockfiles and stages written manifests, changelogs, `pre.json` changes and existing lockfiles before consuming release inputs. It stages consumed changeset and `pre.json` deletions via `git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch` before unlinking those files from disk. If refresh, generated-state staging or input-deletion staging fails, changesets and pre-state deletion inputs remain on disk for retry.\"\n## VER-CAS-06\n113-      \"criterion\": \"A spec that no longer covers the new version is rewritten to it, keeping the operator and precision for Cargo and npm (`^1.2` becomes `^2.0` for 2.0.0), or to the exact version for npm when `preserve-npm-ranges = false`. A runtime, optional, build or peer dependent that is itself released in this run, for any reason, has every such spec on a bumped internal dependency raised to the dependency's new version the same way, even when the spec still covers it (a covering spec that cannot be raised, such as a wildcard or a bare Python requirement, is left unchanged); a dependent that is not releasing keeps its spec unless out of range. `workspace = true`, pnpm rolling `workspace:` shorthands and catalog specs are never rewritten by either rule; an out-of-range pnpm explicit range is rewritten while retaining its `workspace:` protocol and alias. A dev dependent's spec is\n## VER-PRE-08\n188-      \"criterion\": \"A snapshot writes manifests and refreshes each active ecosystem's existing lockfile, unconditionally (there is no `--no-refresh-lockfiles` for `snapshot`), so a subsequent locked install resolves against the snapshot version; it ignores and keeps pending changesets, writes no changelog or `pre.json`, and stages nothing in git; under `--dry-run` it writes nothing.\"\n## VER-APPLY-10\n266-      \"criterion\": \"`version --emit-decision <path>` writes the release decision JSON to `<path>` relative to the workspace root after the plan has been applied successfully: `schemaVersion` 2, a digest, and one entry per canonical manifest of each bumped package (ecosystem-qualified name, target version, reasons) sorted by package. Reason `kind` is `changeset`, `inference`, `fixedGroup` or `linkedGroup` (with `groupId`), `cascade` (with source package and edge kind, `peer` for peer escalation) or `preReleasePolicy` (with the prerelease tag).\"\n## VER-AGG-02\n71-      \"criterion\": \"An entry name resolves to a workspace package by prefixed id (`cargo/foo`) or bare name; a bare name that matches packages in two or more ecosystems aborts the run with an ambiguous-name error (E103).\",\n## VER-PRE-01\n158-      \"criterion\": \"`callisto pre enter <tag>` writes `.changeset/pre.json` with `mode` `pre`, the tag, every package's current version under `initialVersions`, keyed by its display id (`foo`, or `cargo/foo` when another ecosystem has a `foo`) and an empty `changesets` list, then stages the file with git; under `--dry-run` it prints the content and writes nothing. For promoted packages, an older bare key is assigned to the unique historical owner at the commit that added pre.json; if no unique owner exists, version fails with E245.\"\n20:      \"description\": \"Enters or exits prerelease mode by \n109:      \"criterion\": \"Coverage: an exact spec covers only \n113:      \"criterion\": \"A spec that no longer covers the new\n158:      \"criterion\": \"`callisto pre enter <tag>` writes `.\n162:      \"criterion\": \"`pre enter` fails when the tag is em\n179:      \"criterion\": \"A malformed `.changeset/pre.json` (i\n226:      \"criterion\": \"Only a missing file is treated as ab","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3fe0553a-9618-43f7-8a37-e116c9a89694","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:17:39.025Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## VER-CS-07\n57-      \"criterion\": \"Writing fails for an empty summary with entries (E056), an empty package name (E057), or a name containing `\\\"`. A changeset with no entries and no summary writes as an empty file.\",\n## VER-APPLY-08\n258-      \"criterion\": \"Outside pre mode, `version` refreshes affected lockfiles and stages written manifests, changelogs, `pre.json` changes and existing lockfiles before consuming release inputs. It stages consumed changeset and `pre.json` deletions via `git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch` before unlinking those files from disk. If refresh, generated-state staging or input-deletion staging fails, changesets and pre-state deletion inputs remain on disk for retry.\"\n## VER-CAS-06\n113-      \"criterion\": \"A spec that no longer covers the new version is rewritten to it, keeping the operator and precision for Cargo and npm (`^1.2` becomes `^2.0` for 2.0.0), or to the exact version for npm when `preserve-npm-ranges = false`. A runtime, optional, build or peer dependent that is itself released in this run, for any reason, has every such spec on a bumped internal dependency raised to the dependency's new version the same way, even when the spec still covers it (a covering spec that cannot be raised, such as a wildcard or a bare Python requirement, is left unchanged); a dependent that is not releasing keeps its spec unless out of range. `workspace = true`, pnpm rolling `workspace:` shorthands and catalog specs are never rewritten by either rule; an out-of-range pnpm explicit range is rewritten while retaining its `workspace:` protocol and alias. A dev dependent's spec is\n## VER-PRE-08\n188-      \"criterion\": \"A snapshot writes manifests and refreshes each a