{"parentUuid":"edc79726-4f6c-4b40-8132-7b9ac841fb7b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b2969dd6-8ba4-407d-b83e-bb26cef63937","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EbMnfccMf8LH7GZ6Ewiiao","type":"tool_result","content":"## REL-CMD-08\n122-      \"criterion\": \"A malformed `--package` value fails with `E227` and an unknown package with E102. A duplicate selection, a version whose release is complete, or a package with no publish target fails with E169.\",\n## REL-CMD-04\n104-      \"criterion\": \"`callisto release --dry-run` prints each package as `<ecosystem/name> <version>` with its operations (a table on a colour terminal, `Release plan:` lines otherwise) and performs no effect. This holds on a dirty worktree, without an `origin` remote, and in a workspace that needs the CI route. With `--format json` it prints the plan document, whose `digest` equals the receipt's `intentDigest` from a following `callisto release` on the same state; the document carries a sibling `diagnostics` array (e.g. an artifact owner selected without its product) when derivation raised any, and omits the field otherwise. `release plan`'s JSON output carries the same `diagnostics` array; the `--out` file it writes never does.\"\n## REL-PUB-11\n249-      \"criterion\": \"A publish command that fails with auth, rate-limit or other registry output fails the run with E163, and the error carries the last 8 lines of the command's standard output followed by its standard error. A publish run also echoes its standard output to the live log, on stderr. A failing git or gh effect command fails with E164. No effect command is re-issued automatically. Tool output shown in these errors, in the live stderr echo and in JSON errors has credentials masked as `[REDACTED]`: the values of the known credential variables and of any variable named `*_TOKEN`, `*_SECRET` or `*_PASSWORD`, URL userinfo, `npm_`, `ghp_`-family, `github_pat_` and `pypi-` tokens, `Bearer` values, and `.npmrc` `_authToken`, `_auth` and `_password` values.\",\n20:        \"Invalid --package: E227, E102 or E169.\",","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"17a54f0f-d001-4db0-b32b-39c6d4b85ab2","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:18:29.067Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## REL-CMD-08\n122-      \"criterion\": \"A malformed `--package` value fails with `E227` and an unknown package with E102. A duplicate selection, a version whose release is complete, or a package with no publish target fails with E169.\",\n## REL-CMD-04\n104-      \"criterion\": \"`callisto release --dry-run` prints each package as `<ecosystem/name> <version>` with its operations (a table on a colour terminal, `Release plan:` lines otherwise) and performs no effect. This holds on a dirty worktree, without an `origin` remote, and in a workspace that needs the CI route. With `--format json` it prints the plan document, whose `digest` equals the receipt's `intentDigest` from a following `callisto release` on the same state; the document carries a sibling `diagnostics` array (e.g. an artifact owner selected without its product) when derivation raised any, and omits the field otherwise. `release plan`'s JSON output carries the same `diagnostics` array; the `--out` file it writes never does.\"\n## REL-PUB-11\n249-      \"criterion\": \"A publish command that fails with auth, rate-limit or other registry output fails the run with E163, and the error carries the last 8 lines of the command's standard output followed by its standard error. A publish run also echoes its standard output to the live log, on stderr. A failing git or gh effect command fails with E164. No effect command is re-issued automatically. Tool output shown in these errors, in the live stderr echo and in JSON errors has credentials masked as `[REDACTED]`: the values of the known credential variables and of any variable named `*_TOKEN`, `*_SECRET` or `*_PASSWORD`, URL userinfo, `npm_`, `ghp_`-family, `github_pat_` and `pypi-` tokens, `Bearer` values, and `.npmrc` `_a